LinkedHashSet is a class in Java that implements the Set interface and is part of the Java Collections Framework.
 It is a hash table and Doubly linked list implementation of the Set interface,
      which means it maintains the order of elements based on their insertion order.
It is not synchronized (not thread-safe).
LinkedHashSet which allows for efficient insertion, deletion, and search operations while maintaining the order of elements.

Features
     Maintains insertion order
  ✅ Fast (O(1) average)
  ✅ Allows one null
     Uses hashing (refer HashCode_Explanation page)

HashSet:        Hash table only
LinkedHashSet:  Hash table + Doubly Linked List

Head -> First → Second → Third → Tail

